{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791382902,"nonce":"sYc/tbz2JKcpMQR9TJA0he8Jb2E=","title":"Superclass property access bypasses the parent accessor inside an override","message":"Repro: /tmp/SuperPropertyProbe.hx, accepted by native Haxe. Child getters and setters call super.prop, and a function-valued property getter reads super.callback and captures the resulting function. Cranelift compilation reports missing prop/callback storage and then a missing captured inherited variable. The computed properties correctly have no backing fields.\n\nThe accessor recursion guard recognizes the current function name and the this register. A Super receiver uses the same register and accessor name, so it incorrectly bypasses the parent accessor. Super access must dispatch to the parent accessor even from inside the overriding accessor; a direct this access keeps the existing backing-field bypass.\n\nThe same diagnostics prevent unit.MyClass from compiling in TestType, TestSerialize, and TestReflect. Its ChildSuperProp overrides get_prop, set_prop, and get_fProp with super property accesses. Dependent imported-module failures then obscure ordinary fields and constructors. This issue covers the superclass accessor guard; other property issues remain separate.\n\nEvidence: /tmp/rayzor-super-property-native-probe.log and /tmp/rayzor-super-property-baseline-probe.log. Verified checkpoint results will be recorded before closing.","files":null}]}